  "observation": "Cold-boot Kernel menu input paths on both selected original discs reach visible world-map terrain, sky, a flying machine and minimap, and the original Battling menu. That menu has four selectable entries: Bonus Battling, Practice, Tutorial and Exit. Disc 1 recorded branches display Bonus Battling match settings, Practice Gear selection with Weltall and Vierge, a Tutorial arena with instructions, and a return to the original title via Exit. Ordered Up/Left world-map inputs change the rendered machine/world view. The world-map and Battling overlay entry windows match decoded original source resources on both discs.",
  "interpretation": "These add observed world-map and minigame entry points to the coverage inventory, with original mode/overlay provenance. They validate these recorded input paths through the existing Kernel adapter. Dedicated world-map/minigame state setup, target readiness, movement arithmetic, minigame rules, complete location/encounter counts and native gameplay remain unimplemented. Kernel Battle produced flat teal output and Kernel Menu produced black output under reset-default setup; neither is a successful gameplay reference.",
  "confidence": "supported",
  "validation": {
    "preconditions": [
      "Selected measured Disc 1/Disc 2 CHDs; original-source catalogs and scenario adapter from EVID-REF-007",
      "Pinned Nix observation shell with the recorded external core and HLE BIOS",
      "Fresh ignored output directories and no imported checkpoints"
    ],
    "commands": [
      "nix --extra-experimental-features 'nix-command flakes' develop path:./nix#observation",
      "Follow the Kernel route reproduction procedure in tools/reference/README.md using tests/reference-inputs/kernel-mode-observation-route.json. Write each recorded scenario object unchanged to its own local file, invoke scenario.py with that file and the matching original CHD, and use a new output folder per case.",
      "Review the final images and the named navigation/movement step captures against the recorded output descriptions; a completed input program alone is not target-mode readiness.",
      "For the stated world-map and Battling source slots, read the complete 2048-byte logical source-sector extents, verify their catalogued projected-prefix hashes, decode using the independently transcribed original 0x80032eb4 routine described in EVID-REF-007, and compare 128 bytes at decoded offset entry_address - captured_global_0x80018084 with original captured RAM at entry_address & 0x1fffff. Retain original bytes and disassembly locally."
    ],
    "expected": "Recorded Kernel routes produce the independently reviewed visible results, with source-specific original overlay attribution. Unsupported/reset-default Battle and Menu outcomes remain explicit gaps.",
    "actual": "All fifteen bounded cold-boot input programs completed. Parent reviewed the final world-map/Battling/title/flat/black outputs and the navigation/motion captures. The three-down Battling route visibly selected Exit and returned to the title. Exact 128-byte original entry-window source/RAM comparisons passed for Worldmap and Battling on both discs. Battle and Menu did not establish successful target initialization.",
    "result": "passed",
    "tolerance": "Visual entry-point and exact source-entry-window correspondence only. No battle success, minigame rule, target readiness, authoritative coordinate, native runtime or hardware timing equivalence is asserted.",
